{
  "info": {
    "name": "TutorBird API",
    "description": "Unofficial Postman collection for the TutorBird integration API.\n\nTutorBird publishes API keys and a Zapier integration. It does not publish HTTP paths. Requests in **Students**, **Families**, **Calendar**, and **Payments** call `{{baseUrl}}` (default `https://api.tutorbird.com/v1`) using a community mapping of the documented operations. Student, parent, and family routes were confirmed on 2026-10-08 and use PascalCase wire names. Do not use GET /v1 as a health check; it can return HTTP 500 while those routes work. Calendar, payment, and webhook requests are still inferred. Treat a 404 on an inferred path as \"this path is not confirmed,\" not as a bug in your key.\n\nCreate a key in TutorBird under **Business Settings \u2192 Integrations \u2192 + Add API Key**. Choose **Read-Only** for the find requests, or **Read & Write** for Add Student, Update Student, and Add Payment. The key is shown once. Put it in the collection variable `apiKey` or in the TutorBird environment. This collection sends it as `Authorization: Bearer <apiKey>`.\n\n**Webhook samples** post example payloads to `{{webhookSinkUrl}}` so you can try a receiver. They are not sent to TutorBird. Email and SMS samples are empty objects because TutorBird has not published those fields.\n\nSources, retrieved 2026-10-03:\n\n- https://support.tutorbird.com/en/articles/963-how-do-i-integrate-with-zapier\n- https://support.tutorbird.com/en/articles/965-what-can-i-do-with-tutorbird-zapier\n- https://support.tutorbird.com/en/articles/1062-zapier-triggers\n- https://support.tutorbird.com/en/articles/1063-zapier-actions\n- https://zapier.com/apps/tutorbird/integrations\n\nNot affiliated with TutorBird.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{apiKey}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "https://api.tutorbird.com/v1"
    },
    {
      "key": "apiKey",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "studentId",
      "value": "sdt_4f8a21"
    },
    {
      "key": "familyId",
      "value": "fml_91c0ab"
    },
    {
      "key": "eventId",
      "value": "evt_77ab9001"
    },
    {
      "key": "webhookSinkUrl",
      "value": "https://httpbin.org/post"
    },
    {
      "key": "parentId",
      "value": "prt_10aa20"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Students",
      "description": "Zapier keys: `add_student`, `update_student`, `search_student`.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Add student (child)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"FirstName\": \"Maya\",\n  \"LastName\": \"Chen\",\n  \"Status\": \"Trial\",\n  \"Family\": {\n    \"FamilyName\": \"Chen\"\n  },\n  \"Adult\": {},\n  \"Telephone\": {\n    \"TelephoneNumber\": \"+1-416-555-0148\",\n    \"TextingAllowed\": true\n  },\n  \"SkillLevel\": \"Grade 6\",\n  \"LocalSchool\": \"Harbour Elementary\",\n  \"Note\": \"Prefers afternoon lessons\"\n}\n",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/students",
            "description": "Creates a child on a new family.\n\nSend `Family` (`FamilyName` is optional) and `\"Adult\": {}`. Omitting `Adult`, or sending a populated `Adult`, returns HTTP 400 `StudentInputItem.Adult: Must be null for new family`. To join an existing family instead, send `FamilyID` and omit `Family`.\n\n`FirstName` and `LastName` are required (non-empty, max 60). `Status`, `Telephone`, `SkillLevel`, `LocalSchool`, and `Note` persist. Nested `Email` does not persist on create. There is no delete; retire a duplicate with PUT and `{\"Status\": \"Inactive\"}`.\n\nRequires a **Read & Write** key. Success is HTTP 200 and a JSON string of the new `sdt_` id, not an object and not 201. Confirmed 2026-10-08."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Create returned 200', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Create returned a student id string', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.be.a('string').and.match(/^sdt_/);",
                  "});",
                  "if (typeof body === 'string') pm.collectionVariables.set('studentId', body);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Add student (adult)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"FirstName\": \"Jordan\",\n  \"LastName\": \"Hale\",\n  \"Status\": \"Active\",\n  \"Family\": {\n    \"FamilyName\": \"Hale\"\n  },\n  \"Adult\": {},\n  \"Telephone\": {\n    \"TelephoneNumber\": \"+1-289-555-0114\",\n    \"TextingAllowed\": true\n  },\n  \"SkillLevel\": \"Algebra\",\n  \"Note\": \"Evening lessons\"\n}\n",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/students",
            "description": "Creates a student on a new family with the confirmed body: `Family` plus `\"Adult\": {}`.\n\nA separate adult-student type was not confirmed on this route. A populated `Adult` object returns HTTP 400 `StudentInputItem.Adult: Must be null for new family`. Nested `Email` does not persist on create.\n\nRequires a **Read & Write** key. Success is HTTP 200 and a JSON string of the new `sdt_` id. Confirmed 2026-10-08."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Create returned 200', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Create returned a student id string', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.be.a('string').and.match(/^sdt_/);",
                  "});",
                  "if (typeof body === 'string') pm.collectionVariables.set('studentId', body);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Update student",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"Status\": \"Inactive\",\n  \"EmailAddress\": \"maya.chen@example.com\"\n}\n",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/students/{{studentId}}",
            "description": "Partial update. `PUT` returns HTTP 200 and JSON `true`. `PATCH` returns 405.\n\nEmail persists only as flat `EmailAddress`. Nested `Email`, `email`, and `StudentEmail` do not stick. `Status` accepts Active, Inactive, Waiting, Lead, or Trial. There is no delete; `Inactive` retires a duplicate.\n\nRequires a **Read & Write** key. Confirmed 2026-10-08."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Update returned 200', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Update returned true', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.eql(true);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Find student by id",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/students/{{studentId}}",
            "description": "Returns one student (`sdt_`). A read-only key is enough. Confirmed 2026-10-08."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Find returned 200', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Find student by name or email",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/students",
            "description": "Lists every student. A search query string is ignored; `GET /students` returns `ItemSubset` and `TotalItemCount` for the full account. Confirmed 2026-10-08. Use Find student by id when you already have an `sdt_` id."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Find returned 200', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Families",
      "description": "Zapier keys: `search_parent`, `search_parents`.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Find first parent",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/parents?familyId={{familyId}}&first=true&limit=1",
            "description": "Find Parent. The first parent is the one added to the family earliest. You can search by family id, email, or name. Path is inferred."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Find returned 200', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Find all parents",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/parents?familyId={{familyId}}",
            "description": "Find All Parents. The help center says the result is a list, one object per parent, with ids prefixed `prt_`. Path is inferred."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Find returned 200', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Add parent",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"FamilyID\": \"{{familyId}}\",\n  \"FirstName\": \"Elise\",\n  \"LastName\": \"Chen\"\n}\n",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/parents",
            "description": "Creates a parent on an existing family. `FamilyID` must already exist. There is no `POST /families` (404). A new family is created only by `POST /students` with `Family` and `\"Adult\": {}`.\n\n`FirstName` and `LastName` persist. Nested `Email` and `MobileTelephone` on this body do not. Set email afterward with `PUT /parents/{{parentId}}` and flat `EmailAddress`. Parent mobile did not persist via `MobileTelephone`, `TelephoneNumber`, `PhoneNumber`, `MobileTelephoneNumber`, or `MobilePhone`.\n\nRequires a **Read & Write** key. Success is HTTP 200 and a JSON string of the new `prt_` id. Confirmed 2026-10-08."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Create returned 200', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Create returned a parent id string', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.be.a('string').and.match(/^prt_/);",
                  "});",
                  "if (typeof body === 'string') pm.collectionVariables.set('parentId', body);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Update parent",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"EmailAddress\": \"elise.chen@example.com\"\n}\n",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/parents/{{parentId}}",
            "description": "Sets the parent email as flat `EmailAddress`.\n\nMobile does not persist via `MobileTelephone`, `TelephoneNumber`, `PhoneNumber`, `MobileTelephoneNumber`, or `MobilePhone` (known gap). `IsPreferredInvoiceRecipient` did not persist on PUT.\n\nRequires a **Read & Write** key. Confirmed 2026-10-08."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Update returned 200', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
